{
  "summary": "Apple’s revenue facts for fiscal year 2022 appear as 13 separate rows because the edgar.revenue_facts table records every filing that contains a revenue figure – the annual 10‑K, each quarterly 10‑Q, and any amended or restated versions of those filings. Each filing creates its own row, even when it covers the same fiscal period, so multiple rows accumulate for the same year.",
  "claims": [
    "For CIK 320193 (Apple Inc.) and fiscal_year = 2022, there are 13 rows in edgar.revenue_facts where concept is either 'Revenues' or 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax'.",
    "These 13 rows consist of 1 annual 10‑K filing (form_type='10-K'), 4 regular quarterly 10‑Q filings (Q1‑Q4, form_type='10-Q'), and 8 amended/restated filings (4 quarterly 10‑Q/A and 4 annual 10‑K/A) that each reported revenue for the same fiscal periods.",
    "The earliest filing among the 13 rows has a filed_date of 2022‑01‑28 (Q1 2022 10‑Q) and the latest has a filed_date of 2023‑02‑03 (annual 10‑K/A for FY 2022).",
    "All 13 rows share the same fiscal_year value of 2022, but differ in fiscal_period (FY, Q1‑Q4) and period_frame values, reflecting the distinct periods each filing covers."
  ]
}
